& [SAIL] is Semantic Attention and Inference Language
  + [language_identity_uuid] is 0ed05d20-ff22-4418-aaa5-d12a98a33d55
  + [full_name] is Semantic Attention and Inference Language
  + [short_name] is SAIL
  + [role] is the attention-first semantic instruction language of the LLM Semantic Operating System
  + [attention_domain] is observable focus, boundary, outside, priority, transition, reentry, and attention state
  + [inference_domain] is typed association, comparison, decomposition, composition, derivation, validation, reconciliation, and revision
  + [navigation_fit] is SAIL programs navigate semantic structures under purpose without making the navigation metaphor part of primitive semantics
  + [relationship_to_SOP] is SAIL is the candidate attention-first successor foundation; legacy SOP is preserved as migration source and possible verbose surface syntax
  = must: use SAIL as the stable name for new language-foundation work
  - never: imply control of hidden model attention from the name

& [FormationPrecedence] is the authority order between language and database
  + [semantic_authority] is SAIL primitive, state, type, relation, effect, and program contracts
  + [index_authority] is derived searchable records pointing back to signed language and SOP files
  + [feedback] is database retrieval evidence revealing missing identities, ambiguous types, or inadequate language relations
  + [rule] is language semantics lead while database formation begins after the first stable identity contracts
  = must: prevent database convenience from silently redefining language meaning
  = must: use retrieval failures as evidence for a later signed language revision

& [SAILSemanticIndexMinimum] is the smallest database surface needed during language formation
  + [language_element_uuid] is the stable identity of a primitive, operator, function, type, effect, program, library, or legacy mapping
  + [canonical_name] is the exact declared name
  + [normalized_term_set] is lookup forms and aliases
  + [element_kind] is value_kind, state_field, attention_primitive, inference_primitive, control_operator, effect, operator, function, program, library, or migration_rule
  + [purpose_set] is intended uses addressed by the element
  + [input_kind_set] is accepted semantic inputs
  + [output_kind_set] is produced semantic outputs
  + [relation_set] is typed references to related elements
  + [source_file] is the authoritative repository-relative file
  + [source_locator] is the declaration location or content-addressed block
  + [content_digest] is the indexed source identity
  + [authority_state] is canonical, formation, legacy, provisional, stale, or conflicted
  + [indexed_at] is the observed indexing time
  = must: answer exact identity and typed structural lookup before weighted semantic search

& [SAILStructureQuery] is the first searchable interface
  + [query_uuid] is the stable query identity
  + [term_set] is one or more input terms or handles
  + [intended_purpose] is the optional purpose constraint
  + [element_kind_filter] is optional
  + [authority_filter] is optional
  + [repository_scope] is the bounded source set
  + [result] is ranked SAIL elements, legacy SOP structures, file locators, relation paths, and match explanations
  = must: return exact and typed matches before correlation-expanded matches
  = must: expose why each result matched
  - never: treat search rank as specification authority

& [CoformationSequence] is the ordered near-term plan
  + [step_1_name] is settle SAIL identity
  + [step_2_primitives] is test attention and inference primitive minimality
  + [step_3_state] is define AttentionState invariants and transition legality
  + [step_4_IR] is define typed semantic intermediate representation identities
  + [step_5_minimum_index] is create SAILSemanticIndexMinimum schema from stable identities
  + [step_6_seed] is index the SAIL foundation and selected legacy SOP declarations
  + [step_7_query] is prove exact term plus purpose lookup with file citations
  + [step_8_feedback] is record ambiguity, missed retrieval, and language-support gaps
  + [step_9_weights] is add correlation weights only after deterministic lookup works
  + [step_10_faculties] is recompile faculty libraries and index their exported functions
  = must: allow steps 2 through 4 design work and step 5 schema preparation to overlap
  = must: block database implementation until the indexed identities in steps 2 through 4 stabilize

& [CoformationRequirementSet] is the traceable requirement collection
  + [SAIL-001] is name the language Semantic Attention and Inference Language
  + [SAIL-002] is preserve legacy SOP as migration source rather than overwrite it
  + [SAIL-003] is make SAIL semantic identities authoritative over derived database records
  + [SAIL-004] is provide exact and typed structural search before correlation weighting
  + [SAIL-005] is return authoritative file references and match explanations
  + [SAIL-006] is feed retrieval gaps back through source-preserved SJS language revision

& [SJSProcessingTrace] is the coformation trace
  + [fold_1_subject] is SAIL language identity and its subordinate searchable semantic index
  + [fold_2_boundary] is language semantic authority inside SAIL; database-derived search and feedback remain subordinate
  + [fold_3_data_design] is stable language element identity, kind, terms, purpose, signatures, relations, source locator, digest, and authority
  + [fold_4_governance] is semantics lead, deterministic lookup precedes weighted retrieval, and database evidence cannot silently alter language
  + [fold_5_solution_shape] is primitive and state formation followed immediately by minimum index seeding and query proof
  + [fold_6_fault_review] is premature schema lock, database-defined semantics, alias collision, stale source, opaque rank, and weighted search before exact lookup
  + [fold_7_phase_lock] is name and order are stable; primitive and state formation remain the next authority gate

